            <ArticleTitle>Diagnosis of Eagle's syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>575-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of Eagle's syndrome is presented. Although the incidence of styloid process elongation in the population is fairly common, only a small percentage of these patients exhibit symptoms associated with Eagle's syndrome. It is important for the dental practitioner to be aware of this anomaly and to understand its anatomic basis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
